# Cloud Functions environment example. Copy the values you need into
# functions/.env.<your-project-id> (deploy) or functions/.env.local (emulator).
# Both files are ignored by Git. Never commit a real token.

# One-time token for the first-run setup page (/setup). It lets the first
# administrator be created from the web app while no administrator exists.
# Use a random value of at least 16 characters, for example:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# Setup closes automatically once an administrator exists; you may remove the
# value and redeploy afterwards.
SETUP_TOKEN=
